{pad:meta title='Inline debug'/}

<p>{app:tag 'debug'/} shows a value as a collapsible tree in the page, where the template uses
it, and the rendering goes on - unlike {app:tag 'dump'/}, which stops the request.</p>

{common:example 'fragments/debug_1'/}

<ul>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}pad:debug $name/{pad:close/}</code> - one value; an array is a tree to unfold, a missing name says so.</li>
  <li><code>{pad:open/}pad:debug{pad:close/}</code> - every field visible where it stands: the rows of the enclosing levels, innermost first, and the application's variables.</li>
  <li>Only a local request sees it: the command line, or this machine asking itself with nothing forwarded. Anyone else gets nothing, and <code>$padDiagnostics = FALSE</code> switches it off for every web request - the command line still gets it.</li>
</ul>
